2026-11-07T06:49:28.4322730Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T06:49:28.4346210Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T06:49:28.4346900Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T06:49:28.4347420Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T06:49:28.4347650Z 
2026-11-07T06:49:28.4349480Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T06:49:28.4350240Z 
2026-11-07T06:49:28.4350580Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T06:49:28.4351880Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T06:49:28.4352660Z 
2026-11-07T06:49:28.4352960Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T06:49:28.4353310Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T06:49:28.4353650Z 
2026-11-07T06:49:28.4353930Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T06:49:28.4354490Z   $ sh ./install-nix
